WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:07.250
Hey Thoughty2 here and welcome to the Schaerbeek,
one of the nineteen municipalities of Brussels.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:13.469
On the 18th May 2003 Schaerbeek held a location
election using electronic voting machines.

00:00:13.469 --> 00:00:19.240
All was going well until the votes were counted
and it was noticed that one candidate received

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:25.480
4,096 extra votes that couldn't have been
possible, considering the total number of

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.480
voters that attended.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:33.379
This wasn't just a small anomoly, this was
a major hiccup, something had gone seriously

00:00:33.379 --> 00:00:35.320
wrong with the vote.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:39.579
There was a large investigation and the electronic
voting machines used in the election were

00:00:39.579 --> 00:00:41.170
thoroughly checked over.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:45.260
Even the source code for the software was
scrutinised to try and find a bug that would

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:49.679
explain 4,096 votes out of nowhere.

00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:56.430
But it wasn't a software bug, it was caused
by something that no one could have anticipated,

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:00.780
a charged particle from outer space.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:07.619
Several hundred light years away, and hundreds
of years ago a star exploded in a galaxy far,

00:01:07.619 --> 00:01:08.979
far away.

00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:15.380
This violent supernova emitted cosmic rays,
trillions of highly charged particles of matter.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:21.600
They will travel through space indefinitely
at close to the speed of light.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.140
But one of these particles set off on an epic
mission, a lifelong goal it was determined

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:32.579
to achieve: to disrupt the Belgium local elections
of 2003.

00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:38.210
This tiny terrorist traveled through the inky
black for hundreds of years.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:44.130
It finally reached Earth, and in a show of
defience penetrated its magnetic field, before

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:51.220
slamming into a microprocessor in the core
of an electronic voting machine in Brussels.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:59.999
This caused a single bit within the computer's
memory to flip from a 0 to a 1, known as a

00:01:59.999 --> 00:02:05.710
"bit flip" and thus a spectacular chain reaction
happened within the computer's code, which

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:15.130
caused 4,096 votes to materialise from nothing
and register themselves against one particular

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.920
candidate.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.230
If this error hadn't have been noticed by
officials, the wrong candidate would have

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.900
been elected that year.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.510
But this isn't some super-rare event.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:31.400
Planet Earth is constantly being bombarded
by trillions of charged particles from outer

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:37.920
space and your electronic devices are continually
at the mercy of this radiation.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.830
Have you ever been typing up an essay and
just before you hit save your computer freaks

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:46.709
out and you receive the ominous "blue screen
of death"?

00:02:46.709 --> 00:02:53.220
In many such cases it may have been caused
by a charged particle from space hitting your

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:57.190
computer's processor and causing a total system
crash.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:03.360
But it's not just antiquated Window's machines
that suffer from tiny invisible space invaders.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:09.950
Galactic particles cause errors, bugs and
crashes on your smartphones, smart watches,

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:16.069
tablets, televisions and terrifyingly, even
your car's on-board computer.

00:03:16.069 --> 00:03:21.840
In fact such events are so common they have
been given a name, they are called Single

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.420
Event Upsets or an "SEU".

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:31.030
They have been giving computer engineers and
developers a major headache since the dawn

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.890
of computer processors.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:39.510
Forever causing completely unexplainable issues
and crashes that just shouldn't have happened.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:44.301
We could just ignore the issue, after all
we've put up with it for all this time, we

00:03:44.301 --> 00:03:49.640
just get angry when it happens, slam our keyboard
against the wall and continue our day acting

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:54.010
as though a slight computer glitch didn't
get under our skin and cause us to flip the

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:55.410
hell out.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:04:02.390
But we simply can't ignore SEUs, because they
can be deadly.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:10.129
In October 2008 Qantas flight number 72 was
midflight on the way from Singapore to Perth

00:04:10.129 --> 00:04:12.430
Airport in Australia.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:19.500
When suddenly, with no warning the plane's
autopilot system disabled itself, causing

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:27.680
the plane to freefall rapidly, for 23 seconds,
before pilots regained control and safely

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.340
made an emergency landing.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:34.889
One third of the passengers were seriously
injured due to the massive g-force suffered

00:04:34.889 --> 00:04:36.419
from the sudden freefall.

00:04:36.419 --> 00:04:42.320
A lengthy investigation took place and it
was discovered that the autopilot was turned

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:47.229
off by a computer error causes by an SEU.

00:04:47.229 --> 00:04:52.950
The most likely explanation is that a highly
charged particle from a cosmic ray, trillions

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:59.240
of miles away in space had hit the computer's
processor, wreaking havoc.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:04.560
The higher up in the atmostphere you go the
more prone your electronics are to SEUs, because

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:09.640
many of the particles entering Earth are stopped
before they reach the ground.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:13.540
This means planes are particularly at risk.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:19.430
Whether we like it or not our world is run
almost entirely by computers.

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:25.690
Our bank balances are bits on a computer hard
drive, our cars park by themselves and will

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:28.400
very soon drive themselves.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:33.330
Computers power the vast majority of conversations
that take place every day across the globe.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:38.660
Every piece of information we now receive
comes from computers and they influence every

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.289
decision we make.

00:05:40.289 --> 00:05:46.639
So in a world so dependant on computers it's
only a matter of time before an invisible

00:05:46.639 --> 00:05:53.550
cosmic particle causes an SEU somewhere in
the world that completely distrupts a major

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:54.760
computer system.

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:57.990
The fallout could be enormous.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:05.919
Just imagine, if for example a particle caused
an SEU on a major federal server somewhere,

00:06:05.919 --> 00:06:12.449
causing the banks to collapse and the GDP
of the United States to drop from 18 trillion

00:06:12.449 --> 00:06:18.419
dollars to 18 dollars overnight; Trump could
finally lose his shit and nuke the World,

00:06:18.419 --> 00:06:21.820
because of a single atomic particle.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:25.810
Okay I may be hyperbolising, but it could
happen... maybe.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:31.300
So what do we do to defend against these atomic
anarchists?

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:36.880
Well we already are and we have been doing
for almost three decades.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:42.940
In the early 90s IBM and some other computer
manufacturers realised they had to come up

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:47.789
with a way to make computers more reliable
if they were ever going to sell them en-mass

00:06:47.789 --> 00:06:53.170
to consumers and even more so to businesses
who needed servers that they could rely on

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:55.099
24/7.

00:06:55.099 --> 00:07:00.970
So a few tech companies came up with the idea
of parity.

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:05.050
Computers speak in bits, its their language
in its most primitave form.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:11.780
A single bit is the smallest unit of data
in a computer and it can either be a 1 or

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:12.780
a 0.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:18.639
Put all these bits together and suddenly you
have words, for example this may look like

00:07:18.639 --> 00:07:20.110
nonsense to you and I...

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:21.110
01001110 01101111 01100010 01101111 01100100
01111001 00100000 01100101 01111000 01110000

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:22.110
01100101 01100011 01110100 01110011 00100000
01110100 01101000 01100101 00100000 01010011

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:23.110
01110000 01100001 01101110 01101001 01110011
01101000 00100000 01101001 01101110 01110001

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:24.110
01110101 01101001 01110011 01101001 01110100
01101001 01101111 01101110 00101110

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.310
...but to a computer this reads as "Nobody
expects the Spanish inquisition."

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:34.940
Take the first eight numbers "01001110" which
translates as "N", this group of eight bits

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:36.290
is called a byte.

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:43.380
But all it takes is to change the last digit
of this byte from a zero to a one and its

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:48.250
translation changes completely, from an N
to an O.

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:50.119
Now this is where parity comes in.

00:07:50.119 --> 00:07:56.440
Computer scientists had the genius idea of
adding a ninth digit to the end of every byte,

00:07:56.440 --> 00:08:02.120
an extra zero or one, this extra digit is
called a "parity bit".

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:08.740
If all eight digits add up to an even number
then the parity bit will be a zero, representing

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:12.830
even and if not, then a one is added, representing
odd.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:20.599
And therefore you know it's a valid byte,
if a byte is received by the computer's processor

00:08:20.599 --> 00:08:25.629
that adds up to an odd number but the parity
bit is a zero, suggesting it should have added

00:08:25.629 --> 00:08:31.479
up to an even number, then the computer instantly
knows that there's an error in the byte, potentially

00:08:31.479 --> 00:08:34.480
caused by an SEU.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:38.940
But merely detecting errors wasn't enough.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:48.590
It's not just cosmic radiation that's corrupting
memory but nearby magnetic fields and the

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:53.770
ironising background radiation of the Earth
itself.

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:58.890
Even the temperature of the room the computer
sits in can create software hiccups and cause

00:08:58.890 --> 00:08:59.890
crashes.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:05.240
So people with really long beards, because
as we all know, you're not a computer scientist

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.720
unless you have an impressive beard, ladies
excluded.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:15.480
Took parity bits one step further and invented
a genius way for computers to not only detect

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:19.570
when an error has occured but self-correct
it.

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:25.840
. and so ECC memory was born, short for error-correcting
code memory.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:31.460
When an error is detected via a byte's parity
bit the ECC memory goes back to the code that

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:37.340
created the byte and double checks everything
using special algorithms.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:42.450
Once it has discovered what the true value
should have been, it simply corrects it quietly

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:47.961
and gets on with its life and the human behind
the screen is non-the-wiser that their computer

00:09:47.961 --> 00:09:53.430
just saved them from a blue screen of death
and a whole load of stress.

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:58.470
So if this miraculous ECC memory exists then
why does my computer, smartphone and tablet

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:03.860
still crash occasionally and why are planes
falling out of the sky?

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:10.270
Well ECC memory is slighly more expensive
than regular, non-ECC memory, so most consumer

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:15.780
computers are built with non-ECC memory, meaning
they can't self-correct.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:21.821
ECC memory is typically used in mission critical
applications for example by banks, and in

00:10:21.821 --> 00:10:28.030
server farms where abosolute reliability is
essential to their business and a minute of

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:32.760
downtime could literally cost millions of
dollars.

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:36.800
And yes I know what you're thinking, they
didn't think that the the lives of hundreds

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:44.790
of humans on a plane didn't warrant ECC memory,
but financial trading does, yeah.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:50.710
Don't worry, since that incident, the reliability
of on-board aeroplane computers has been significantly

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:51.710
improved.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:58.620
But even with ECC memory in your computer
you're not immune to crashes, far from it.

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:04.890
It can protect you from cosmic rays and radiation,
sure, but some crashes are simply caused by

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:10.381
poor and shoddy programming, or software that's
riddled with bugs, and there's plenty of that

00:11:10.381 --> 00:11:11.720
to go around.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:18.180
So we've found a solution to cosmic ray bombardment
here on Earth but the problem is a thousand

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:22.600
times worse once you leave Earth's protective
atmostphere.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:28.830
Out in space the amount of cosmic ray abuse
one suffers is many thousands of times higher.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:33.180
Apollo astronauts reported seeing a streak
of white light across their field of vision

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:36.890
every 3 minutes, whilst out in space.

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:39.040
Even when they closed their eyes.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:44.800
It was explained to them that this was caused
by cosmic rays hitting their optic nerve,

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:48.740
causing it to temporarily glitch and crash.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:54.100
As you can imagine cosmic rays play havoc
with satellites and spacecraft, but they can

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:56.540
also save them.

00:11:56.540 --> 00:12:03.140
In 2015 the privately funded space exploration
programme "The Planetary Society" launched

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:09.930
a groundbreaking data-gathering spacecraft
into space, called LightSail, that would use

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:16.830
a large, reflective sail to propel itself
through space using photons emitted from the

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:17.860
Sun.

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:24.740
But soon after it reached outer space the
onboard software crashed and LightSail ceased

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:28.700
all communication with Earth.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:33.140
The engineers back on Earth knew that the
crash was caused by a memory leak and all

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:37.110
that was needed was a total system reboot.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:43.860
See, even rocket scientists fix their computer
issues by turning it off and back on again.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:49.660
For eight days the spacecraft drifted through
space, completely dead.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:56.800
The engineers had almost lost hope, when suddenly,
a cosmic ray from a galaxy many millions of

00:12:56.800 --> 00:13:03.730
miles away, hit the on-board microprocessor
in just the right place, which caused the

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:05.950
software to reboot itself.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:11.310
The engineers were amazed that suddenly they
were receiving messages once again from the

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.020
craft.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:23.750
There are over 4,500 artificial satellites
currently orbiting Earth and they are crucial

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:25.910
to our every day life in the modern age.

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:31.930
We use them for navigation, to predict the
weather, for business and finance, communication,

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:33.970
television and many other uses.

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:38.700
It's therefore of the upmost important that
they don't crash on us.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:43.670
They use a multitude of techniques to do this,
such as physical shielding using thick, heavy

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:46.860
metals and ECC memory.

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:52.580
NASA however were so concerned about the threat
of cosmic rays upon their spacecraft's on-board

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:59.200
computers that they devised a devastatingly
simple yet enormously effective solution to

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:02.600
solve the problem once and for all.

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:08.880
Instead of putting one processor chip inside
the craft they put three identical chips in

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:09.880
there.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:16.040
When the computer needs to calculate something
it is calculated on all three processors simitaneously

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:23.450
and the results are compared, if one processor
produces a different result from the other

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:26.640
two then the computer knows it's wrong.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:33.510
The likelyhood of a cosmic ray causing an
SEU on one processor out in space is quite

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:39.250
high, but the chance of it happening to two
or more processors at the same time and causing

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:47.330
the exact same error is vanishingly small,
making the three processor solution extremely

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.190
reliable.

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:55.370
Which just goes to show that sometimes the
most complex of problems requires the simplest

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:56.370
of solutions.

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:58.640
Thanks for watching.

